/// What a generated command method needs from the connection.
///
/// Named `invoke`, not `call`: a Dart class with a `call` method becomes
/// callable as a function, and a connection object that can be invoked like
/// a closure is a surprise nobody asked for.
abstract interface class CatsCommandTransport {
  /// Sends [name] with [params], correlated by a generated id, and completes
  /// with the reply's `data` (null when the command returns none).
  ///
  /// Throws on an `ok: false` reply, on timeout, and on disconnect — every
  /// pending call must fail when the socket dies, or a leaked completer is a
  /// spinner that never stops.
  Future<Object?> invoke(String name, Object? params);
}

